# Revisions to skip when running git blame.
#
# Both are mechanical reformats that touch nearly every line without changing
# what any of it means. Verified rather than assumed: across the six documents
# the Prettier commit reflowed, the prose is word-for-word identical — the only
# non-whitespace changes are table separator padding and emphasis markers, which
# render the same. Reflowing prose is no more a content change than rewrapping a
# method signature.
#
# Without this file they sit on top of every blame result, hiding the commit that
# actually explains each line.
#
# Enable locally with Scripts/setup-dev.sh, or:
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# GitHub, GitLab and Rider honour the file automatically.

